    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="0797" n="787" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg787"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6–1049: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister-Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-10T20:00:00+08:00">June 10, 1949—8 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 11—7:09 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 560. Assume Department aware Chinese Government has finalized purchase
                    second lot Mexican silver (Cantel 523, June 3) value US $7.1 million. Central
                    Bank official stated today all available US dollar deposits now exhausted.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clark</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
